\begin_layout Plain Layout
 
\series bold
Economic KKT cookbook.
\series default
 For 
\begin_inset Formula $\max_{x\ge0}f(x)$
\end_inset

 subject to 
\begin_inset Formula $Ax\le b$
\end_inset

, use 
\begin_inset Formula \[
0\le x\perp A^\top\lambda-\nabla f(x)\ge0,
\;
0\le\lambda\perp b-Ax\ge0.
\]
\end_inset

Here 
\begin_inset Formula $a\perp z$
\end_inset

 means 
\begin_inset Formula $a_i z_i=0$
\end_inset

 component by component. Guess the positive choices and binding resource constraints, solve their equalities, and then verify every remaining inequality. Once 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda$
\end_inset

 is known, the envelope theorem gives 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{b_j}=\lambda_j$
\end_inset

 wherever the value function is differentiable. 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


