\begin_layout Standard
A consumer has date-0 wealth 
\begin_inset Formula $w=24$
\end_inset

 and consumes only at date 1. She invests 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\ge0$
\end_inset

 dollars in a risky asset and 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta\ge0$
\end_inset

 dollars in a safe asset, subject to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\alpha+\beta\le24.
\]
\end_inset

The safe asset has gross return 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

. The risky asset has gross return 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\widetilde R=
\begin{cases}
\tfrac12,&\text{in state }L\text{, with probability }\tfrac12,\\[2pt]
\tfrac74,&\text{in state }H\text{, with probability }\tfrac12.
\end{cases}
\]
\end_inset

Borrowing and short selling are not allowed. Her Bernoulli utility is 
\begin_inset Formula $u(c)=\sqrt c$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

